Host-side tests for the rppico fastloader timing
================================================

src/rppico/llfl-common.c implements the timing interface used by the
low-level fastloader code (src/llfl/) with busy-waits on the CPU cycle
counter. This test compiles it for the host against the shims in
shims/, which replace the cycle counter, the bus inputs and the bus
outputs with a simulation in llfltest.c: reading the cycle counter or
the inputs advances the simulated time, the inputs follow a waveform
of that time, and every line change is recorded with its time.

Covered:

  - generic 2-bit send (JiffyDOS timing) for all byte values: both
    lines of a pair change in the same write, no earlier than the
    requested time and at most 40 cycles later, with interrupts
    disabled
  - a NO_WAIT change that is applied by llfl_teardown, and restoring
    the interrupt state
  - generic 2-bit receive for all byte values
  - all of the above with cycle counter wrap during the transfer
  - a reference time set by the caller (as the FC3 sender does)
  - ATN abort while waiting for a line, flagging of late changes

The bus protocol of the individual loaders and the real pin timing
still need testing on hardware.

Running the tests
-----------------

    make check      builds and runs the tests, plain and with
                    ASan/UBSan
    make clean      removes build/
